{"title":"Regression Analysis","markdown":{"headingText":"Regression Analysis","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n## SLR\n\n::: callout-important\n## Summary of Simple Linear Regression (SLR)\n\n**1) The PRF :** $y_i =\\alpha +\\beta x_i +\\epsilon_i$\n\n**2) The OLS estimates of** $\\alpha$ **and** $\\beta$ **are:**\n\n$$a=\\bar y-b \\bar x$$\n\n$$b=\\frac{n\\sum xy-(\\sum x)(\\sum y)}{n\\sum x^2 -(\\sum x)^2}$$\n\nrespectively.\n\nHence the **estimated regression line** is:\\\n\n$$\\hat y_i =a+bx$$\n\n**3) Point prediction:** For a given value of $X$ say $x_g$ the predicted value of $Y$ is:\n\n$$\\hat y_g=a+b *(x_g)$$\n\n**4) Goodness of fit for SLR:**\n\n$$R^2=\\frac{b^2(\\sum x^2 -n \\  \\bar x^2)}{\\sum y^2 -n \\ \\ \\bar y^2}\\ \\ ; \\ \\ 0\\le R^2\\le 1$$\n\n**5) Mean squared error (MSE): as an estimate of** $\\sigma_e^2$:\n\n$$s_e^2=\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} (y_i -\\hat y_i)^2}{n-2}$$\n\n**6) Hypothesis test for** $\\beta$**:**\n\n$$H_0: \\beta =c \\ \\ vs.$$\n\n$$H_1: \\beta \\ne c$$\n\nTest statistic:\n\n$$t_0=\\frac{b-c}{s.e(b)}$$\n\nwhere, $s.e(b)=\\frac{s_e}{\\sqrt {\\sum (x-\\bar x)^2}}$\n\nUnder $H_0$, $t_0$ follows *T*-*distribution with* $n-2$ df.\n:::\n\n**Problem 7.1 [@walpole2017,pp.399]:** The following is a portion of a classic data set called the “pilot plot data” in Fitting Equations to Data by Daniel and Wood, published in 1971. The response y is the acid content of material produced by titration, whereas the regressor x is the organic acid content produced by extraction and weighing.\\\n\n|       |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |     |\n|:-----:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **y** | 76  | 62  | 66  | 58  | 88  | 70  | 37  | 82  | 88  | 43  |\n| **x** | 123 | 55  | 100 | 75  | 159 | 109 | 48  | 138 | 164 | 28  |\n\n```{r}\n# Define the function\nget_slr_stats <- function(x, y) {\n  # Basic counts and sums\n  n <- length(x)\n  sum_x <- sum(x)\n  sum_y <- sum(y)\n  sum_x2 <- sum(x^2)\n  sum_y2 <- sum(y^2)\n  sum_xy <- sum(x * y)\n  \n  \n  x_bar <- mean(x)\n  y_bar <- mean(y)\n  \n  slope <- (n * sum_xy - (sum_x * sum_y)) / (n * sum_x2 - (sum_x^2))\n  \n  intercept <- y_bar - (slope * x_bar)\n  \n  # Return results as a named list\n  return(list(\n    n = n,\n    sum_x = sum_x,\n    sum_y = sum_y,\n    sum_x2 = sum_x2,\n    sum_y2 = sum_y2,\n    sum_xy = sum_xy,\n    x_bar = x_bar,\n    y_bar = y_bar,\n    intercept = intercept,\n    slope = slope\n  ))\n}\n```\n\n```{r}\n# Creating the data frame\ndf <- data.frame(\n  y = c(76, 62, 66, 58, 88, 70, 37, 82, 88, 43),\n  x = c(123, 55, 100, 75, 159, 109, 48, 138, 164, 28)\n)\n\n# Display the data frame\n#print(df)\nstats <- get_slr_stats(df$x, df$y)\n#print(stats)\n\n#summary(lm(df$y~df$x))\n\n```\n\n## MLR\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":false,"output":true,"warning":false,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"message":false,"engine":"knitr"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-extern